"""
Tutorial 3 — synthesize the continuous LQG regulator.

Weights follow Bryson's rule: each diagonal entry is `1 / (largest acceptable
deviation)^2`, in that channel's own units. The rule exists because the channels are
not commensurable — thrust is newtons while the surfaces are degrees, so a uniform
penalty makes thrust ~10^6 times more expensive than it should be and the synthesis
returns a controller with no usable throttle.

  q1  (controlled outputs)          q2  (control inputs)
    yalt    0.5 m                     uT     20000 N
    ypitch  5 deg                     uEl    10 deg
    yvt     1 m/s                     uAil   10 deg
    yalpha  2 deg                     uRud   10 deg
    ybeta   2 deg                     uLef   10 deg
    yQ      10 deg/s

`yn`/`ye` carry only a placeholder 1e-6 (the solver rejects a zero entry): north and
east position have no equilibrium in forward flight, so regulating them to a fixed
reference asks for something the airframe cannot do — the error grows with distance
flown until it dominates the cost and the loop departs. Position belongs to an outer
guidance loop, not to this inner regulator.
"""
analysis TutorialLQG
  extends DyadControlSystems.LQGAnalysis(measurement = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "yphi", "ypitch", "ypsi", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yP", "yQ", "yR"], controlled_output = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "ypitch", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yQ"], control_input = ["uT", "uEl", "uAil", "uRud", "uLef"], loop_openings = [], q1_diag = [1e-6, 1e-6, 4.0, 131.312, 1.0, 820.702, 820.702, 32.8281], q2_diag = [2.5e-9, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01], r1_diag = [0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01], r2_diag = [0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01], duration = -1.0)
  model = LQGDemo()
relations
end

"""
Tutorial 3b — the same LQG design, ZOH-discretized at `ControllerTs` (100 Hz).

Produces the sampled-data controller that tutorial 4 simulates. Discretizing here —
rather than applying `c2d` to the continuous result afterwards — keeps one design as
the single source of truth for both loops.
"""
analysis TutorialDiscreteLQG
  extends DyadControlSystems.LQGAnalysis(measurement = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "yphi", "ypitch", "ypsi", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yP", "yQ", "yR"], controlled_output = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "ypitch", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yQ"], control_input = ["uT", "uEl", "uAil", "uRud", "uLef"], loop_openings = [], q1_diag = [1e-6, 1e-6, 4.0, 131.312, 1.0, 820.702, 820.702, 32.8281], q2_diag = [2.5e-9, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01], r1_diag = [0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01], r2_diag = [0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01], duration = -1.0, disc = "zoh", Ts = ControllerTs)
  model = LQGDemo()
relations
end